A function $g$ from the integers to the integers is defined as follows:
\[g(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n + 5 & \text{if $n$ is odd}, \\
n/2 & \text{if $n$ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]
Suppose $m$ is odd and $g(g(g(m))) = 65.$ Find $m.$

If \(x=3\) and \(y=4\), express the value of the following as a common fraction: \[
\frac
{~\frac{1}{y}~}
{\frac{1}{x}}
\]

Let $a_0 = -3, b_0 = 2$, and for $n \geq 0$, let
\begin{align*}
a_{n+1} &= 2a_n + 2b_n + \sqrt{a_n^2 + b_n^2}, \\
b_{n+1} &= 2a_n + 2b_n - \sqrt{a_n^2 + b_n^2}.
\end{align*}
Find $\frac{1}{a_{2012}} + \frac{1}{b_{2012}}.$

Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
2x^2 - 4 & \text{ if } x < 10, \\
x - 20 & \text{ if } x \geq 10.
\end{array}
\right.\] What is $f(f(f(25)))$?

Let \[g(x) =
\begin{cases}
3x + 4 &\text{if } x < 0, \\
x^2 + 2x + 1 &\text{if } x \geq 0.
\end{cases}
\] Find $g(-3)$.

Find an ordered pair \((x, y)\) that satisfies both of the following equations: 
\begin{align*}
3x - 4y &= -7, \\
4x + 5y &= 23.
\end{align*}

For real numbers $x$, define the piecewise function:
\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x+4 &\text{ if }x>4, \\
3x+b &\text{ if }x\le 4.
\end{array}
\right.\]
What must the value of $b$ be to ensure that the function $f(x)$ is continuous?

If \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
x^2 - 9 &\quad \text{if } x \ge -3, \\
x + 6 &\quad \text{otherwise},
\end{cases}
\]then for how many values of $x$ is $f(f(x)) = 0$?

Let \[g(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl} 
x^2 + 2x - 5 & \text{ if } x < 5, \\
2x - 18 & \text{ if } x \geq 5.
\end{array}
\right.\] 
What is $g(g(g(15)))$?

Express as a common fraction in simplest form: $$
\sqrt{7\frac{9}{16}}
$$

Given the graph of a function, $y=G(x)$:

[asy]
import graph; size(8cm); real lsf=0.5; pen dps=linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10); defaultpen(dps); pen ds=black; real xmin=-4.5,xmax=4.5,ymin=-0.99,ymax=6.5;

pen cqcqcq=rgb(0.75,0.75,0.75);
/*grid*/ pen gs=linewidth(0.7)+cqcqcq+linetype("2 2"); real gx=1,gy=1;
for(real i=ceil(xmin/gx)*gx;i<=floor(xmax/gx)*gx;i+=gx) draw((i,ymin)--(i,ymax),gs); for(real i=ceil(ymin/gy)*gy;i<=floor(ymax/gy)*gy;i+=gy) draw((xmin,i)--(xmax,i),gs);

Label laxis; laxis.p=fontsize(10);

xaxis("",xmin,xmax,Ticks(laxis,Step=1.0,Size=2,NoZero),Arrows(6),above=true); yaxis("",ymin,ymax,Ticks(laxis,Step=1.0,Size=2,NoZero),Arrows(6),above=true);
real f2(real x){return 1.2*sqrt(abs(x+1.5))+(7/pi)*atan(1.1*sqrt(abs(x+1.5)));}
draw(graph(f2,xmin,xmax),linewidth(1));
clip((xmin,ymin)--(xmin,ymax)--(xmax,ymax)--(xmax,ymin)--cycle);
label("$y=G(x)$",(xmax+0.25,f2(xmax)),E);
[/asy]

The graph describes the function $G(x) = 1.2 \sqrt{\left| x+1.5 \right|} + \frac{7}{\pi} \arctan(1.1\sqrt{\left| x+1.5 \right|})$. Calculate $G(2)$, assuming it results in an integer.

Let $h(x)$ be a function piecewise defined as \[h(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
-x & x\le 0, \\
3x-50 & x>0.
\end{array}
\right.\] If $a$ is negative, find $a$ so that $h(h(h(15)))=h(h(h(a)))$.

