Sarah, Bob, and Alice paint a very long picket fence.
Sarah starts with the first picket and paints every $s$ th picket;
Bob starts with the second picket and paints every $b$ th picket;
Alice starts with the fourth picket and paints every $a$ th picket.
Call the positive integer $1000s+100b+10a$ paintable when the triple $(s,b,a)$ of positive integers results in every picket being painted exactly once by only one of them. Find the sum of all paintable integers.

The graph of $y = g(x)$ is as follows:

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

real func(real x) {
  real y;
  if (x >= -3 && x <= 0) {y = -2 - x;}
  if (x >= 0 && x <= 2) {y = sqrt(4 - (x - 2)^2) - 2;}
  if (x >= 2 && x <= 3) {y = 2*(x - 2);}
  return(y);
}

int i;

for (i = -5; i <= 5; ++i) {
